    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe application returns owners as an `OwnerDto` (generated from `openapi.yml`) populated by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`. To expose the new `initials` field, I made two small, well-placed changes:\n\n1. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added `getInitials()` as a derived attribute alongside the `firstName`/`lastName` fields it depends on. A tiny private `initial(...)` helper upper-cases the first letter and appends a dot, and `getInitials()` concatenates them (e.g. `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`). It guards against null/empty names.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, mirroring the existing `displayName` precedent, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nNo mapper change was needed: MapStruct auto-maps `initials` by name from `Owner.getInitials()` to the DTO. Putting the computation on `Person` (rather than in the mapper) keeps the logic with the data it derives from and makes it reusable for any `Person` subtype \u2014 while `displayName`'s formatting stays a mapper concern as before.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
